WEBVTT

00:30.322 --> 00:33.951
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

00:44.044 --> 00:46.837
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION - SOME
SCENES WERE GENERATED USING AI

00:46.838 --> 00:49.048
CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
WERE FILMED SAFELY

00:53.011 --> 00:54.012
Hwayeong.

02:19.681 --> 02:21.515
Power off.

02:21.516 --> 02:23.060
Just listen to it.

02:25.771 --> 02:28.272
Come on, just try listening to it for now.

02:28.273 --> 02:30.359
Music is good for treating anxiety.

02:31.318 --> 02:32.735
It's out of battery.

02:32.736 --> 02:34.279
Huh?

02:34.905 --> 02:38.199
I charged it yesterday, though.
Give me a second.

02:38.200 --> 02:40.661
- I should have a power bank.
-  …is now departing.

02:41.244 --> 02:42.663
Do you want to chew on this?

02:44.164 --> 02:47.250
Chewing on something can help you relax.

02:50.754 --> 02:52.506
I told you I'm okay.

02:53.590 --> 02:55.550
You're not okay, though.

02:56.385 --> 02:58.719
You were crying yesterday.

02:58.720 --> 03:01.847
Excuse me, please wake up.

03:01.848 --> 03:03.307
Seonu…

03:03.308 --> 03:04.309
Sorry?

03:06.895 --> 03:07.896
Seonu…

03:09.272 --> 03:10.524
You were saying "Seonu."

03:19.616 --> 03:20.826
Do you know me?

03:21.618 --> 03:22.910
Sorry?

03:22.911 --> 03:24.579
Did I ever ask for your help?

03:26.331 --> 03:27.332
Ah…

03:27.916 --> 03:30.084
Well, no, but I--

03:30.085 --> 03:33.004
I'm sorry you had to help me
like that yesterday, but…

03:34.423 --> 03:35.841
I never asked for your help.

03:37.300 --> 03:40.095
So just be on your way
and stop crossing the line.

03:40.971 --> 03:42.347
What?
:cue

03:46.601 --> 03:49.687
Wait, when did I ever cross the…

03:50.981 --> 03:52.566
Excuse me!

04:01.241 --> 04:02.367
What the hell? Sheesh.

04:03.743 --> 04:08.205
Hey, I need to get on a ferry right away,
so I'm going to need a prescription.

04:08.206 --> 04:09.999
I'll head to your hospital.

04:10.000 --> 04:11.668
I'm heading over right now.

04:14.463 --> 04:15.963
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

04:15.964 --> 04:18.090
The last ferry came
and went ages ago.

04:18.091 --> 04:20.342
How come Dr. Do Jiui still isn't here?

04:20.343 --> 04:24.388
I know. He couldn't have deserted his post
on his first day, right?

04:24.389 --> 04:26.599
- Sheesh.
- By the way, Ms. Hwang,

04:26.600 --> 04:28.684
a newbie is joining us next week, right?

04:28.685 --> 04:32.062
I'm going to be really nice to her.

04:32.063 --> 04:33.273
Newbie?

04:34.149 --> 04:38.194
You said the new nurse
is in her third year. I'm in my fourth.

04:38.195 --> 04:40.279
Doesn't that make her the newbie?

04:40.280 --> 04:42.740
I guess you're right,

04:42.741 --> 04:45.451
but she won't be your typical newbie,
just so you know.

04:45.452 --> 04:47.620
She hasn't even been a nurse
for that long,

04:47.621 --> 04:49.497
so imagine how awkward she'll feel.

04:49.498 --> 04:51.373
I should help her out.

04:51.374 --> 04:54.585
I've even organized
all the handover notes.

04:54.586 --> 04:57.923
Oh, okay. Well done.

04:58.757 --> 05:02.051
As to who will end up helping whom,
we won't know until she gets here,

05:02.052 --> 05:03.719
but well done.

05:03.720 --> 05:05.596
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

05:05.597 --> 05:07.056
Dr. Do.

05:07.057 --> 05:08.808
Hmm, what?

05:08.809 --> 05:12.895
Goodness, Dr. Do!
Do you have any idea what time…

05:12.896 --> 05:17.441
My gosh. You look like death.
What happened to you?

05:17.442 --> 05:20.445
I'm sorry. I fell asleep on the ferry.

05:21.363 --> 05:24.032
So you were sleeping on the ferry
all this time?

05:25.367 --> 05:26.450
Yes.

05:26.451 --> 05:29.662
Must be nice being
that unbothered.

05:29.663 --> 05:32.082
Sleeping fine while ditching work.

05:42.676 --> 05:45.011
Do you want to chew on this?

05:45.595 --> 05:48.473
Chewing on something can help you relax.

05:48.974 --> 05:51.017
FEELING DOWN?
HERE'S A PICK-ME-UP!

06:07.701 --> 06:13.581
EPISODE 2
THE WOMAN WHO CROSSES THE LINE

06:16.543 --> 06:18.794
-  Bellflower roots?
- That's right.

06:18.795 --> 06:22.089
- They're precious wild bellflower roots.
- Mmm.

06:22.090 --> 06:25.092
So, about that…
You saved the chief's life last week,

06:25.093 --> 06:28.263
so the youth association
told me to give it to you.

06:29.055 --> 06:31.432
It's from the youth association?
Thank you.

06:35.604 --> 06:38.689
By the way, Mr. Lee Jangsu,
what brings you in today?

06:38.690 --> 06:42.610
I'm just here
to get those meds I always take.

06:42.611 --> 06:44.904
Those meds you always take?

06:47.741 --> 06:50.326
You already took
two weeks' worth a week ago.

06:50.327 --> 06:53.662
Two weeks' worth
will barely cut it anymore.

06:53.663 --> 06:56.749
My wife also takes it and all,

06:56.750 --> 07:00.545
so give us about
a month's worth this time.

07:01.129 --> 07:04.048
Did you just say you share your meds
with your wife?

07:04.049 --> 07:05.758
Yes.

07:05.759 --> 07:07.760
No. Proxy prescriptions are illegal.

07:07.761 --> 07:10.220
Strictly speaking,
it's not a proxy prescription,

07:10.221 --> 07:12.765
since I'm also taking those meds.

07:12.766 --> 07:13.849
I still can't do it.

07:13.850 --> 07:17.519
And the coughing might turn into pneumonia
if it continues for two weeks or more,

07:17.520 --> 07:19.146
so I'll give you three days' worth.

07:19.147 --> 07:20.939
Come back after finishing it.

07:20.940 --> 07:23.025
I'm busy as hell because of the anchovies!

07:23.026 --> 07:25.278
And you expect me to visit regularly?

07:25.904 --> 07:28.656
That's the only way I can properly
assess your condition, sir.

07:28.657 --> 07:31.909
I know my condition best.
:cue

07:31.910 --> 07:33.619
I'll take care of myself,

07:33.620 --> 07:35.205
so just give me 30 days' worth.

07:36.498 --> 07:38.582
- I can't do that.
- That's how it's always been!

07:38.583 --> 07:40.501
You're just going to cut me off like this?

07:40.502 --> 07:42.961
Cough medicine,
something for your phlegm,

07:42.962 --> 07:46.048
antibiotics, and this long one is
the stomach coating agent.

07:46.049 --> 07:49.635
Take one packet in the morning
and in the evening after a meal.

07:49.636 --> 07:53.098
Did you really
only put three days' worth in there?

07:55.016 --> 07:58.602
We only put in
as much as the doctor prescribed.

07:58.603 --> 08:01.021
That's the law.

08:01.022 --> 08:04.942
Is there a law saying
civil servants can ignore residents?

08:04.943 --> 08:07.361
Who said anything about ignoring anyone?

08:07.362 --> 08:10.698
That's not it. It's just how the law is.

08:10.699 --> 08:12.408
Hey, you think I don't know the law?

08:12.409 --> 08:14.035
Law this, law that!

08:14.619 --> 08:18.372
Looks like I'll have to take legal action
against you civil servants

08:18.373 --> 08:20.457
who love the law so much
as a wake-up call!

08:20.458 --> 08:21.625
Wait!

08:21.626 --> 08:24.879
Have you been drinking?
Calm down a little, so I can explain…

08:32.512 --> 08:34.222
- What should we do?
- Sorry?

08:34.806 --> 08:38.559
Word is Mr. Lee actually went to
the county office to file a complaint.

08:38.560 --> 08:39.768
Ah.

08:39.769 --> 08:42.397
Looks like things will get
quite troublesome for a while.

08:46.192 --> 08:49.195
Doc, loosen up a little, will you?

08:49.863 --> 08:53.825
Duking it out with the residents
is never easy.

08:54.409 --> 08:56.118
It can't be helped.

08:56.119 --> 08:58.455
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you.

08:59.330 --> 09:01.082
Which brings us to my point.

09:01.666 --> 09:05.252
If it won't be a big issue,
how about we just do as they ask?

09:05.253 --> 09:07.004
That's better for everyone, no?

09:07.005 --> 09:10.549
Giving patients
whatever prescriptions they ask for

09:10.550 --> 09:12.509
isn't necessarily "better for everyone."

09:12.510 --> 09:14.512
Nothing good comes
from giving in to patients.

09:17.724 --> 09:19.767
I'm not saying this for my own good, okay?

09:19.768 --> 09:21.602
It's because I'm worried about you guys.

09:21.603 --> 09:23.353
If you keep doing as you please,

09:23.354 --> 09:25.565
something terrible is
going to happen to you!

09:26.107 --> 09:27.775
You'll see once it happens to you.

09:27.776 --> 09:29.485
- Gosh, so frustrating.
- What do you…

09:29.486 --> 09:30.569
Is anyone in?

09:30.570 --> 09:32.238
-  Oh, my!
-  Huh?

09:32.989 --> 09:34.240
Oh, goodness!

09:35.408 --> 09:37.076
I see you were still eating.

09:37.077 --> 09:38.327
- Hello.
-  Goodness.

09:38.328 --> 09:41.080
You were discharged
from the hospital already?

09:41.081 --> 09:42.247
Yes.

09:42.248 --> 09:45.125
I got treated right away, after all.

09:45.126 --> 09:48.629
Dr. Do's stubbornness saved my life.

09:48.630 --> 09:53.467
Had it not been for Dr. Do Jiui,
I'd be on my way to Heaven by now.

09:55.261 --> 09:57.305
My, my, my.

09:58.765 --> 10:01.433
Isn't this monkfish liver?

10:01.434 --> 10:02.976
What a precious treat!

10:02.977 --> 10:05.604
Not as precious as my own life.

10:08.691 --> 10:10.735
Goodness, Dr. Do.

10:11.444 --> 10:13.278
Thank you so much.

10:13.279 --> 10:16.907
Once I make a full recovery,
I'll pay you back for everything.

10:16.908 --> 10:18.450
You can count on it.

10:18.451 --> 10:19.494
Okay.

10:20.078 --> 10:23.080
We took too much of your time
when you were eating.

10:23.081 --> 10:25.332
- Let's go now, Chunsik.
- That's right.

10:25.333 --> 10:27.668
You must be tired
since you just got discharged,

10:27.669 --> 10:30.295
- so go home to rest up.
- Okay.

10:30.296 --> 10:32.923
- Thank you, everyone.
- Goodbye.

10:32.924 --> 10:36.677
- Take care.
-  Oh my, thank you.

10:36.678 --> 10:39.012
- Have a safe trip home.
-  Sure.

10:39.013 --> 10:40.639
I love you, Dr. Do.

10:40.640 --> 10:41.723
What?

10:41.724 --> 10:44.602
You're totally
in the chief's good graces now.

10:45.270 --> 10:48.021
On this island,
once you get on his good side,

10:48.022 --> 10:49.982
your quality of life skyrockets.

10:49.983 --> 10:52.442
Last time, he brought me pizza
from the mainland

10:52.443 --> 10:54.320
because he liked my acupuncture treatment.

10:55.029 --> 10:57.114
I got pizza for acupuncture,

10:57.115 --> 11:00.325
so can you imagine how well
he'd treat you for saving his life?

11:00.326 --> 11:01.493
Pizza?

11:01.494 --> 11:03.871
Just because
he liked your acupuncture treatment?

11:03.872 --> 11:05.415
Yes! Pizza!

11:11.129 --> 11:12.714
What the heck?
:cue

11:15.175 --> 11:17.927
Let's see…

11:30.648 --> 11:33.150
Ms. Eom. What's going on here?

11:33.151 --> 11:34.359
What now?

11:34.360 --> 11:37.238
I mean your slippers.
They're the same as mine.

11:38.531 --> 11:41.074
Did you pay a premium
for the overseas shipping too?

11:41.075 --> 11:44.078
I heard these were really hard to get.

11:44.954 --> 11:46.748
A premium?

11:48.917 --> 11:49.918
Let me see now.

11:52.128 --> 11:54.713
Did they always have this color?

11:54.714 --> 11:56.632
I've never seen it before.

11:56.633 --> 11:59.886
What are you, a detective?
What are you looking at my feet for?

12:00.470 --> 12:02.722
I'm just fascinated, that's all.

12:03.389 --> 12:06.099
I think we have pretty similar taste.

12:06.100 --> 12:07.726
Similar, my ass.

12:07.727 --> 12:11.189
How could I possibly have similar taste
to someone who owns a clinic in Seoul?

12:12.357 --> 12:13.650
Just get back to work!

12:17.528 --> 12:20.782
He's such a weirdo!

12:22.116 --> 12:23.409
Damn it!

12:24.953 --> 12:28.080
Who the hell pays a premium
for a flimsy pair of slippers?

12:28.081 --> 12:33.044
I do not like him one bit.

12:50.353 --> 12:51.728
I'm so hungry.

12:59.362 --> 13:02.906
It's only 8:00 p.m.,
but none of the stores are open…

13:02.907 --> 13:04.700
Our island only has
one supermarket.

13:04.701 --> 13:06.451
Ours doesn't even open
at times.

13:06.452 --> 13:08.996
I realized the value
of convenience stores.

13:08.997 --> 13:11.540
If you come across these
on your next trip to the market,

13:11.541 --> 13:13.000
you have to stockpile them.

13:13.001 --> 13:17.254
They rarely stock up on beer,
so finders keepers.

13:17.255 --> 13:18.797
I should rush over there now!

13:18.798 --> 13:21.049
Some beer to keep me company
on these long nights!

13:21.050 --> 13:23.386
Oh, beer…

13:24.929 --> 13:26.639
Beer.

13:31.227 --> 13:34.397
They don't have any ales or IPAs, though.

13:36.816 --> 13:39.359
I wonder if the chief
would get some for me.

13:41.320 --> 13:44.448
Hey, I got here first.
You can't just take them all like that.

13:44.449 --> 13:46.324
- Hey…
- Granny, put these on my tab!

13:46.325 --> 13:47.451
Okay.

13:47.452 --> 13:48.745
Goodbye!

13:49.454 --> 13:52.289
Excuse me, do you have any more beer?

13:52.290 --> 13:53.540
No, that was it.

13:53.541 --> 13:55.126
Wow, I can't even.

13:56.085 --> 13:57.295
What the hell?

14:00.381 --> 14:03.384
LUCKY SUPERMARKET

14:06.763 --> 14:07.930
Mmm.

14:09.640 --> 14:11.017
You drink every day?

14:11.684 --> 14:15.021
Man, what's that voice I hear?
It seems to be crossing a line.

14:16.773 --> 14:20.276
You probably shouldn't be drinking.
If you drink like that every day…

14:23.821 --> 14:25.614
It's just bad for you.

14:25.615 --> 14:28.742
I'm guessing that's a roundabout way
of telling me to hand some over.

14:28.743 --> 14:30.535
But stop crossing the line, okay?

14:30.536 --> 14:32.580
- That's not it. I just--
- Hey.

14:35.041 --> 14:36.959
Do you know how suspicious you are?

14:37.960 --> 14:39.044
What do you mean?

14:39.045 --> 14:41.380
I mean, why do we keep
running into each other?

14:42.590 --> 14:43.925
Are you…

14:44.425 --> 14:46.301
a stalker?

14:46.302 --> 14:48.054
A stalker?

14:49.514 --> 14:52.057
Listen, you're the one
who's always butting in, okay?

14:52.058 --> 14:54.518
I boarded the ferry first,
and I also came here first.

14:54.519 --> 14:56.228
So if we're talking about stalking,

14:56.229 --> 14:57.980
I'd say you fit the profile more.

14:59.440 --> 15:00.441
If not, never mind.

15:01.901 --> 15:02.902
"If not, never"…

15:25.800 --> 15:27.885
Look at me. I almost crossed the line.

15:36.394 --> 15:38.771
:cue

15:50.074 --> 15:51.534
What the hell?

15:53.786 --> 15:54.787
Hello.

15:55.371 --> 15:57.957
So she's a nurse.

15:59.000 --> 16:00.876
Say hello, everyone.

16:00.877 --> 16:02.627
This is Ms. Yuk Hari.

16:02.628 --> 16:06.631
I'm Eom Jeongseon, a fourth-year nurse.

16:06.632 --> 16:08.800
You're third-year… so, class of '19?

16:08.801 --> 16:10.343
I was in the class of '18.

16:10.344 --> 16:13.763
Yes, class of '19.
I'm sure I have a lot to learn from you.

16:13.764 --> 16:16.224
Right. I look forward to working with you.

16:16.225 --> 16:18.226
A lot to learn from her? Please.

16:18.227 --> 16:22.981
Ms. Hari here is an intellectual who used
to work in a university hospital's ER.

16:22.982 --> 16:25.025
Not just any hospital, but Asong Hospital.

16:25.026 --> 16:28.486
I'm sure the operating room
was practically her living room.

16:28.487 --> 16:31.740
But still, isn't this her first time
at a public health center?

16:31.741 --> 16:34.367
Mmm. It may be her first time,

16:34.368 --> 16:37.120
but ever since she was a kid,
she visited the island every holiday,

16:37.121 --> 16:39.539
so she's well-acquainted with Pyeondongdo.

16:39.540 --> 16:43.335
Wow, then you must be
really close to the villagers here.

16:43.336 --> 16:44.753
That's great.

16:44.754 --> 16:47.881
I think it's way harder
to get close to the villagers here

16:47.882 --> 16:49.424
than it is to work here.

16:49.425 --> 16:51.885
That's because you slack off all the time.

16:51.886 --> 16:54.095
I'm Yong Jucheon
of the Korean Medicine Ward.

16:54.096 --> 16:56.765
I look forward
to working with you.

16:56.766 --> 17:00.769
And this here is Dr. Do Jiui, the surgeon.

17:00.770 --> 17:05.440
He's the very man
you busted your ass carrying over here.

17:07.526 --> 17:09.236
So you're a doctor.

17:09.237 --> 17:10.321
Uh, yes.

17:11.155 --> 17:12.490
Huh?

17:13.282 --> 17:15.408
Have you already greeted each other?

17:16.786 --> 17:21.039
Well, I don't know if I can say that.

17:21.040 --> 17:22.625
It might be crossing a line.

17:23.793 --> 17:25.503
What are you talking about?

17:29.131 --> 17:30.258
I'm Hyeon Chiyeon.

17:31.050 --> 17:32.843
I look forward to working with you.

17:33.511 --> 17:35.971
Now then, doctors,
please get ready to see patients.

17:35.972 --> 17:37.681
- Okay.
- As for us,

17:37.682 --> 17:40.351
let me just pull you aside
for a quick chat. This way.

17:41.143 --> 17:42.770
Never expected to see her here.

17:43.271 --> 17:45.689
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

17:47.858 --> 17:53.238
My, you used to be so tiny,
but you've grown so much.

17:53.239 --> 17:56.576
But why did you come here
from such a good university hospital?

17:57.201 --> 17:58.202
Ah…

17:58.953 --> 18:00.537
Well…

18:00.538 --> 18:04.499
I was just wondering why you came
all the way to this island from the city.

18:04.500 --> 18:05.960
If there was a story behind it.

18:07.253 --> 18:10.131
- I just wanted to take a break.
- Mmm.

18:10.840 --> 18:12.299
Take a break?

18:12.300 --> 18:13.466
Right.

18:13.467 --> 18:15.010
Let's do that.

18:15.011 --> 18:17.679
- Take it slow and easy.
-  Mmm.

18:19.181 --> 18:22.601
- Let's catch up again later.
- Uh-huh.

18:23.811 --> 18:27.230
This is Hwang Sinhye from
the Public Health Center speaking.

18:27.231 --> 18:33.361
Though working here may look peaceful,
it's actually a war zone,

18:33.362 --> 18:37.574
and the work we do is just as complicated
as working in an operating room.

18:37.575 --> 18:40.243
It's not the kind of place
where you can just take a break,

18:40.244 --> 18:41.995
is all I'm saying.

18:41.996 --> 18:44.956
I see.
I look forward to your guidance.

18:44.957 --> 18:46.291
- Mm-hmm.
- Ah!

18:46.292 --> 18:47.668
What should I do first?

18:48.919 --> 18:49.920
Ooh…

18:52.298 --> 18:55.551
Why don't you start by switching out
the toilet paper rolls in the bathroom?

18:56.135 --> 18:57.136
Ah…

18:58.012 --> 18:59.013
Toilet paper?

19:01.432 --> 19:03.267
Okay.

19:04.226 --> 19:05.810
- This way?
- Mm-hmm.

19:10.900 --> 19:14.403
Why on earth did I mention toilet paper,
after putting on such a front?

19:35.383 --> 19:37.051
Of all people, why…

19:38.219 --> 19:41.054
Dr. Jiui, you're going to
have to go somewhere.

19:41.055 --> 19:43.640
It's a patient who just had
a cancer operation,

19:43.641 --> 19:45.725
but his daughter's
having trouble reaching him.

19:45.726 --> 19:47.561
She's asking if we can check in on him.

19:48.729 --> 19:51.523
- Me?
- Who else? Should I go?

19:51.524 --> 19:53.274
I don't know my way around yet.

19:53.275 --> 19:56.195
Don't worry about that.
We'll send another person with you.

19:56.779 --> 19:58.530
All settled, right? Mm-mmm.

20:00.950 --> 20:01.992
:cue

20:15.423 --> 20:16.841
Oh, gosh.

20:34.150 --> 20:35.317
Easy, easy!

20:37.403 --> 20:38.446
Seriously…

20:39.155 --> 20:40.238
Hello!

20:40.239 --> 20:42.532
Hey!
Looks like it's starting to drizzle.

20:42.533 --> 20:43.700
I know, right?

20:43.701 --> 20:46.578
Sir, you said it was nearby.
Why do we need a boat?

20:46.579 --> 20:48.831
It's only five minutes away by boat.

20:49.498 --> 20:50.623
Oh, come on…

20:50.624 --> 20:52.250
What business do you have there?

20:52.251 --> 20:54.836
A patient's guardian
requested a home visit.

20:54.837 --> 20:56.921
A patient on that side? Who's sick?

20:56.922 --> 20:58.506
Do you know Mr. Kim Jeongbae?

20:58.507 --> 21:00.217
Kim Jeongbae? Who could that be?

21:01.051 --> 21:03.136
Oh, that guy?

21:03.137 --> 21:05.764
I guess it's the guy who keeps to himself.

21:05.765 --> 21:08.642
But I don't think it'll be easy
getting in that house.

21:09.226 --> 21:12.688
The guy seemed to really hate
people entering his house.

21:13.272 --> 21:14.439
Oh…

21:14.440 --> 21:16.567
So he hates it when people cross the line,

21:17.401 --> 21:18.652
like someone I know.

21:19.153 --> 21:20.236
What?

21:20.237 --> 21:22.947
Ah, it's nothing.
We can go there now, right?

21:22.948 --> 21:24.992
- Of course. Get in.
-  Wait.

21:26.202 --> 21:29.078
Isn't there
some other way there?

21:29.079 --> 21:30.539
Some other way?

21:31.874 --> 21:34.209
Well, they are connected.

21:34.210 --> 21:37.587
But if you were to walk,
it would take at least 40 minutes.

21:37.588 --> 21:40.006
With the mountain path
being really hilly and all.

21:40.007 --> 21:42.884
Who would be dumb enough to do that?

21:44.553 --> 21:47.097
Forty minutes? Okay.

21:47.765 --> 21:50.642
Wait, Dr. Do. You're going to walk there?

21:50.643 --> 21:53.645
You take the boat.
I'll walk. See you there.

21:53.646 --> 21:55.730
Wait…

21:55.731 --> 21:57.274
Doctor!

22:00.319 --> 22:02.738
Where the heck am I? Damn it.

22:08.327 --> 22:09.787
Hey, wait up.

22:14.834 --> 22:17.126
We could have been there
in five minutes.

22:17.127 --> 22:19.045
Why punish ourselves by walking there?

22:19.046 --> 22:21.756
I never asked you to come with me, okay?

22:21.757 --> 22:23.967
You could have just taken the boat.

22:23.968 --> 22:26.719
It's not like there's anything I can do
without a doctor.

22:26.720 --> 22:28.681
Why should I go there by myself?

22:31.308 --> 22:32.309
I was talking to myself.

22:35.104 --> 22:38.106
Tells me not to cross the line
but gives me so many causes for concern.

22:38.107 --> 22:39.816
- Ms. Yuk.
- Okay, okay.

22:39.817 --> 22:41.568
I'll stop talking to myself.

22:41.569 --> 22:44.154
Hurry up.

22:53.956 --> 22:57.041
Haven't you been here before, Ms. Hari?

22:57.042 --> 22:59.295
Who would walk here?
Everyone takes a boat.

23:00.754 --> 23:01.755
Let me see.

23:09.847 --> 23:11.140
Hey, will you please…

23:11.724 --> 23:14.184
That's not it. Your shoulder, Dr. Do…

23:15.144 --> 23:16.269
What about my shoulder?

23:16.270 --> 23:17.271
The other side…

23:18.647 --> 23:19.690
What is it?

23:20.274 --> 23:22.901
Uh… You know what? Never mind.

23:22.902 --> 23:26.196
You think helping is crossing a line,
so I'm not going to say anything.

23:27.573 --> 23:30.034
- But that's going to bite, though.
- What?

23:34.872 --> 23:37.832
Don't move. It's venomous.

23:37.833 --> 23:41.336
Help me with this. Now!

23:41.337 --> 23:45.590
I want to help, but I have to be careful.

23:45.591 --> 23:46.759
What?

23:47.343 --> 23:49.636
You see,
I learned something thanks to you.

23:49.637 --> 23:52.013
No matter how much someone's struggling,

23:52.014 --> 23:55.266
helping when they don't ask for it
is crossing a line.

23:55.267 --> 23:57.936
It's trying to get in!

23:57.937 --> 23:59.187
Hurry and do something!

23:59.188 --> 24:00.898
What can I do? I can't cross the line.

24:01.982 --> 24:04.108
-  Cross it.
- What?

24:04.109 --> 24:06.445
Please cross the line!

24:07.029 --> 24:08.696
- Damn it…
- Cross it?

24:08.697 --> 24:11.324
Cross it. It just crawled inside!

24:11.325 --> 24:12.951
- Get it out.
- Just so we're clear,

24:12.952 --> 24:14.327
you said to cross it.

24:14.328 --> 24:17.080
Put your hands inside and take it out.

24:17.081 --> 24:19.123
It's way inside!

24:19.124 --> 24:20.792
- Lower!
- Where? Okay.

24:20.793 --> 24:22.835
- Oh, come on!
- Okay.

24:25.255 --> 24:27.840
- It's not there. What?
- Uh, Ms. Hari, it went down.

24:27.841 --> 24:28.925
Right now…

24:28.926 --> 24:31.678
- Left waist!
- Darn it!
:cue

24:31.679 --> 24:32.971
Stand still!

24:32.972 --> 24:34.514
Oh, come on!

24:34.515 --> 24:36.641
I think it bit me.

24:36.642 --> 24:37.643
That was my nail.

24:38.978 --> 24:40.853
Stop playing around, seriously!

24:40.854 --> 24:42.105
I'm not.

24:42.106 --> 24:45.109
Oh, oh! Here it is. Hold still.

24:46.151 --> 24:47.987
- I caught it.
- You caught it?

24:51.240 --> 24:53.032
Shouldn't we trap that guy somewhere?

24:53.033 --> 24:55.326
You said it's venomous.
What if it bites someone?

24:55.327 --> 24:56.911
- Why would we do that?
- Damn it.

24:56.912 --> 24:59.331
They don't bite if you leave them alone.

25:01.709 --> 25:04.628
Dr. Do, you owe me one now.
Pay me back later.

25:07.297 --> 25:08.673
But…

25:08.674 --> 25:10.259
But that guy's venomous.

25:12.886 --> 25:15.513
Its fangs were terrifying. Did you see?

25:23.188 --> 25:24.982
This place…

25:29.194 --> 25:30.529
This is…

25:36.368 --> 25:39.078
Uh, are you sure this is the place?

25:39.079 --> 25:40.913
It doesn't look like anyone lives here.

25:40.914 --> 25:43.042
This has to be the place.

25:44.793 --> 25:46.586
Just a second.

25:47.755 --> 25:49.964
DO NOT ENTER

25:51.717 --> 25:55.929
Mr. Kim Jeongbae,
we're here from the public health center.

25:57.264 --> 25:59.099
Mr. Kim Jeongbae, are you home?

26:02.478 --> 26:04.563
I'm pretty sure this is the place.

26:05.814 --> 26:07.774
Hold on.

26:07.775 --> 26:10.736
Are you going in?
That would be a bad idea.

26:11.320 --> 26:14.031
She said it's a patient
who was treated for cancer recently.

26:15.074 --> 26:18.576
If you're going to cross any lines,
you have to make it count.

26:18.577 --> 26:20.162
Especially when saving someone.

26:29.463 --> 26:31.548
Oh, man…

26:32.299 --> 26:34.258
Hey, Ms. Yuk?

26:34.259 --> 26:36.427
It doesn't look like anyone's here,

26:36.428 --> 26:38.221
so let's come back for them next time.

26:38.222 --> 26:40.182
- Mr. Kim Jeongbae!
- Come on.

26:40.724 --> 26:42.267
Mr. Kim Jeongbae?

26:45.270 --> 26:46.354
Let's go inside.

26:46.355 --> 26:48.272
Wait, Ms. Yuk. Why would you go in there?

26:48.273 --> 26:50.526
How dare you enter my home
without permission?

26:52.653 --> 26:53.821
Who the hell are you?

26:54.655 --> 26:56.656
We're from the Public Health Center.

26:56.657 --> 26:59.575
Your daughter said
she couldn't get in touch with you--

26:59.576 --> 27:00.994
Get lost!

27:01.745 --> 27:02.830
Yes, sir.

27:04.665 --> 27:08.251
Now that we know he's fine, let's go.
Hurry up.

27:08.252 --> 27:11.295
Since we're here,
how about a simple checkup? I think that…

27:11.296 --> 27:13.172
What else do we need to check?

27:13.173 --> 27:14.591
…would be a good idea.

27:17.261 --> 27:18.262
But…

27:18.887 --> 27:20.389
he's smoking.

27:25.102 --> 27:26.103
Sir.

27:26.770 --> 27:31.440
I heard you recently had surgery,
but you're smoking right now.

27:31.441 --> 27:35.404
That's why your daughter was so worried
and called us.

27:37.531 --> 27:38.532
So what?

27:39.157 --> 27:41.076
Get the hell out before you regret it.

27:43.245 --> 27:45.705
We have to go, Ms. Yuk.

27:45.706 --> 27:48.000
- I feel sorry for your daughter.
- Ms. Yuk?

27:49.042 --> 27:52.628
She's been losing sleep over her dad,
who doesn't even care about his own life.

27:52.629 --> 27:54.882
Why get the surgery
if you're going to act like this?

27:59.344 --> 28:02.013
I'm going to contact your daughter.

28:02.014 --> 28:04.348
She needs to know
what kind of state her dad's in.

28:04.349 --> 28:07.728
That way, she'll get to decide
whether to give up on her dad or not.

28:18.113 --> 28:20.531
Say one word to my daughter,

28:20.532 --> 28:22.325
- and I'll really kill you.
- Whoa! Sir!

28:22.326 --> 28:24.911
I guess you are ashamed,
seeing as you're angry.

28:24.912 --> 28:27.079
We're sorry. Come with me, Ms. Yuk.

28:27.080 --> 28:28.873
- Sorry, sir.
- I'm not done talking!

28:28.874 --> 28:30.791
-  Hurry up!
-  What are you doing?

28:30.792 --> 28:32.711
What's wrong with you?

28:33.378 --> 28:35.046
- What?
- Come with me.

28:35.047 --> 28:36.923
What on earth are you doing right now?

28:36.924 --> 28:38.007
What?

28:38.008 --> 28:42.219
Don't you know that bringing up smoking
with a cancer patient only riles them up?

28:42.220 --> 28:43.889
I'm just frustrated!

28:46.224 --> 28:47.392
Why would it make you…

28:48.852 --> 28:50.144
:cue

28:59.571 --> 29:02.741
Hey, what was that about earlier?

29:06.078 --> 29:08.288
That man still has a chance.

29:10.332 --> 29:15.212
How could someone try so hard
to ruin a second chance at life like that?

29:16.046 --> 29:19.049
Not everyone can get a second chance.

29:19.841 --> 29:23.387
Some people try their hardest to live,
but end up dying anyway.

29:24.554 --> 29:26.431
If I were that man…

29:27.933 --> 29:30.226
I'd try to live seeing only good things,

29:30.227 --> 29:32.437
doing good deeds,
and thinking good thoughts.

29:34.064 --> 29:35.607
So I can live for a long time.

29:46.618 --> 29:48.704
CHAVOXIFEN
CHAVOXIFEN CITRATE

29:55.127 --> 29:57.336
There must be a way.

29:57.337 --> 29:58.922
There's no such thing.

29:59.756 --> 30:01.590
That's not true. It's too soon to--

30:01.591 --> 30:03.759
What can we do now? The sun's gone down.

30:03.760 --> 30:05.970
What?

30:05.971 --> 30:08.473
I think we're lost.

30:09.516 --> 30:11.350
What?

30:11.351 --> 30:13.103
- Oh, crap!
- Right?

30:17.482 --> 30:18.774
Huh?

30:18.775 --> 30:20.276
What do we do?

30:20.277 --> 30:22.611
Why are you asking me that?

30:22.612 --> 30:25.197
Oh, man…

30:29.911 --> 30:30.912
Oh…

30:35.083 --> 30:36.584
- What is that?
- What is it?

30:36.585 --> 30:38.544
Never mind.
I thought it was something else.

30:38.545 --> 30:39.546
Come on!

30:43.008 --> 30:46.010
Aim the flashlight properly!

30:46.011 --> 30:48.054
You should be aiming it properly, okay?

30:48.055 --> 30:51.849
Didn't you learn in science class
that you're supposed to raise it high

30:51.850 --> 30:53.893
so that the light spreads more?

30:53.894 --> 30:54.977
Darn it…

30:54.978 --> 30:59.024
How can you talk science when you
can't even see what's under your feet?

31:00.484 --> 31:02.235
Are you sure we're going the right way?

31:02.903 --> 31:03.904
Oh…

31:04.488 --> 31:07.407
I think I saw this tree earlier.

31:08.825 --> 31:10.952
Is this place haunted by ghosts?

31:11.495 --> 31:14.413
That's strange.
I thought we were going the right way.

31:14.414 --> 31:16.249
Ghosts?

31:17.417 --> 31:18.709
Yes, ghosts.

31:18.710 --> 31:20.504
Oh, come on! You scared me!

31:21.171 --> 31:23.672
Is my face really that scary?

31:23.673 --> 31:25.550
I've seen worse, but I'm bearing with it.

31:27.761 --> 31:31.347
I don't think
we'll find our way out at this rate.

31:31.348 --> 31:32.891
Let's split up and look around.

31:34.184 --> 31:35.267
Hey.

31:36.812 --> 31:38.187
Ms. Yuk!

31:38.188 --> 31:41.441
Uh, split up? I don't want to!

31:42.275 --> 31:45.027
I don't want that.
Let's stay together.

31:45.028 --> 31:47.696
We won't find the way like this, so--

31:47.697 --> 31:49.116
Let's just stay together.

31:52.035 --> 31:53.453
Is it because you're scared?

31:57.916 --> 32:01.794
Wow, it's one thing
after another with you.

32:04.965 --> 32:06.550
- Oh…
- Huh?

32:18.145 --> 32:21.231
-  Dr. Chiyeon!
- What are you doing here?

32:22.107 --> 32:23.567
You didn't return, so here I am.

32:24.276 --> 32:27.027
With the sun setting
and the boats no longer running.

32:27.028 --> 32:30.240
Man, I'm so relieved.

32:39.374 --> 32:40.584
- Hop on.
- Okay.

32:44.212 --> 32:47.340
Oh… How should I get on?

32:49.342 --> 32:50.719
Should I get on down there?

32:51.344 --> 32:52.887
Okay. Sure.

32:52.888 --> 32:54.305
Keep backing up.

32:54.306 --> 32:56.515
Good, just like that.

32:56.516 --> 32:58.476
Yes, just keep backing up.

33:00.437 --> 33:02.062
But are you sure I can get on?
:cue

33:02.063 --> 33:03.814
I don't think I'd fit.

33:03.815 --> 33:05.901
Another ride will come.
This is a two-seater.

33:06.610 --> 33:09.279
- Wait a second!
- I'll see you later.

33:09.905 --> 33:11.572
I said wait a second!

33:11.573 --> 33:12.824
Take me with you!

33:14.075 --> 33:15.076
Hey!

33:16.244 --> 33:17.453
I'm scared!

33:17.454 --> 33:18.538
Come on.

33:25.337 --> 33:27.171
Are you sure he'll be okay?

33:27.172 --> 33:28.923
He seems to be a scaredy-cat.

33:28.924 --> 33:30.217
He's a big boy.

33:31.468 --> 33:33.261
- Hold on tight.
- What?

33:34.262 --> 33:35.347
Oh, okay.

33:39.309 --> 33:41.937
- Not there. I meant the handles.
- What?

33:43.980 --> 33:46.358
Oh. Um, uh, right.

33:48.443 --> 33:50.862
You still have a habit
of jumping to conclusions.

33:51.905 --> 33:53.405
Excuse me?

33:53.406 --> 33:55.158
Do you really not remember me?

33:57.827 --> 33:58.912
Wait.

34:08.213 --> 34:09.506
Oh…

34:10.340 --> 34:11.341
I'm sorry.

34:12.092 --> 34:13.592
What?

34:13.593 --> 34:14.970
I have a boyfriend.

34:16.304 --> 34:18.890
- Hey, wait--
- I told you I have a boyfriend.

34:29.025 --> 34:30.360
CLIFFSIDE RAW FISH RESTAURANT

34:35.657 --> 34:37.909
Just tell me, okay?

34:40.370 --> 34:41.579
If you buy me a meal.

34:42.205 --> 34:43.206
What?

34:44.457 --> 34:47.919
Come on. We've met before?

34:56.928 --> 34:58.429
- Hello.
-  You're here?

34:58.430 --> 34:59.514
- Hey.
- Auntie!

35:02.267 --> 35:03.351
Dr. Do.

35:06.021 --> 35:07.731
How did you get here so fast?

35:09.065 --> 35:10.066
Thanks to you…

35:10.859 --> 35:12.527
I almost ended up dying, okay?

35:16.072 --> 35:18.449
Ma'am, go slower!

35:18.450 --> 35:20.035
Go slower!

35:24.205 --> 35:26.207
Slower!

35:29.502 --> 35:32.921
It was seriously a white-knuckle ride.

35:32.922 --> 35:35.049
Cheer…  …up!

35:35.050 --> 35:36.134
Here.

35:37.427 --> 35:38.428
You're drinking?

35:39.137 --> 35:41.222
You're meant to drink on days like this.

35:42.098 --> 35:43.557
You're here?

35:43.558 --> 35:44.976
-  Yes.
- Hey, welcome.

35:45.644 --> 35:46.645
What's this?

35:47.812 --> 35:49.271
Oh, my.

35:49.272 --> 35:52.608
I see Dr. Stickler was here.

35:52.609 --> 35:55.527
The great doctor who won't give
proper prescriptions

35:55.528 --> 35:57.946
because he suspects
his patients of foul play.

35:57.947 --> 35:59.324
That's right.

36:00.283 --> 36:05.537
You see, just like you have your rules,

36:05.538 --> 36:08.124
we have our own rules here in Pyeondongdo.

36:08.750 --> 36:10.459
For every new arrival,

36:10.460 --> 36:14.213
our youth association determines
who's the senior and the junior

36:14.214 --> 36:16.716
by having a drink-off.

36:17.342 --> 36:19.927
Whoever gets wasted first
becomes the junior,

36:19.928 --> 36:22.681
and must obey the senior's every word.

36:23.264 --> 36:24.474
See where this is going?

36:25.266 --> 36:27.893
That's why the owner here
is my big sister now.

36:27.894 --> 36:30.312
- Right.
- Geumja, my sis!

36:30.313 --> 36:31.397
Gosh, that's so gross.

36:35.068 --> 36:38.696
What do you say?
Would you, Dr. Stickler-for-the-Rules,

36:38.697 --> 36:42.492
like to partake in our ritual
so we can establish a proper hierarchy?

36:45.120 --> 36:46.203
Well…

36:46.204 --> 36:49.164
I guess he doesn't have
what it takes.

36:49.165 --> 36:51.041
Is it because all he's done is study?

36:51.042 --> 36:53.503
He's a total nerd.

36:56.047 --> 36:57.966
- Let's just go.
- Yeah, let's go.

36:58.550 --> 37:01.176
We have to get back quickly--

37:01.177 --> 37:03.221
If those are the rules here,
I'll give it a go.

37:04.222 --> 37:05.807
Dr. Do, no…

37:06.474 --> 37:07.809
You mean it?

37:08.309 --> 37:09.602
Yes.

37:11.020 --> 37:12.021
:cue

37:15.275 --> 37:18.611
Those guys, they're not human
when it comes to booze, okay?

37:19.154 --> 37:21.364
They're hounds. Boozehounds.

37:22.490 --> 37:24.367
Gosh, I'm so worried.

37:26.202 --> 37:29.497
A man should be able to drink this much.
Don't you think so?

37:46.639 --> 37:48.475
This here's a creamy soju.

38:23.176 --> 38:26.845
I'm not like him.

38:26.846 --> 38:27.847
Not bad.

38:28.348 --> 38:29.933
You can actually hold your liquor.

38:40.109 --> 38:41.944
You haven't forgotten, have you?

38:41.945 --> 38:43.403
The rules in Pyeondongdo.

38:43.404 --> 38:46.198
Whoever loses this
has to become an obedient little bro.

38:46.199 --> 38:49.117
I'm very curious

38:49.118 --> 38:53.664
how much of an obedient little bro
Dr. Stickler over here will be

38:53.665 --> 38:55.374
once I beat him.

39:15.603 --> 39:17.021
I'm also curious…

39:19.524 --> 39:21.275
Wow, look at him go!

39:21.276 --> 39:22.901
…what I'm like when I'm drunk.

39:22.902 --> 39:29.200
2013 HANGUK UNIVERSITY
PRE-MED SEMESTER KICK-OFF PARTY

39:38.710 --> 39:39.794
He won.

39:40.336 --> 39:41.671
He actually won.

39:43.131 --> 39:44.841
Mm-hmm.

39:47.468 --> 39:48.469
Another?

39:53.600 --> 39:56.352
What the…

39:57.061 --> 39:58.521
Do you know who I am?

39:59.522 --> 40:02.108
I'm the Bloodstained Fist
of Pyeondongdo, you prick!

40:06.487 --> 40:07.779
Huh?

40:07.780 --> 40:09.657
Blood…

40:28.801 --> 40:31.845
What's this?

40:31.846 --> 40:34.057
What happened to my hand?

40:41.022 --> 40:42.482
Forceps, please.

40:51.658 --> 40:53.700
Looks like you can feel your hand.

40:53.701 --> 40:54.953
What should we do?

40:55.620 --> 40:59.040
I think we can stitch him up.
There doesn't seem to be any nerve damage.

40:59.707 --> 41:01.292
You're going to stitch him up?

41:02.085 --> 41:05.295
Out of the question. We had alcohol.

41:05.296 --> 41:07.673
This could cause huge problems
down the line,
:cue

41:07.674 --> 41:09.509
and it has happened before.

41:12.929 --> 41:16.556
Article 7 of the code of medical ethics.
A physician shall not practice medicine

41:16.557 --> 41:19.643
while under the influence
of alcohol, narcotics, or drugs,

41:19.644 --> 41:23.022
or in a physical or mental state
that may cause harm to the patient's life

41:23.815 --> 41:25.023
or physical well-being.

41:25.024 --> 41:27.609
If they complain later
that a drunk doctor operated on him,

41:27.610 --> 41:29.278
you'll both be in big trouble.

41:30.989 --> 41:33.281
Let's have him go
to the hospital early tomorrow.

41:36.411 --> 41:38.287
He definitely won't go.

41:39.163 --> 41:40.915
The boats head out tomorrow,

41:41.541 --> 41:44.711
and missing just a single day
is a huge loss in anchovy fishing.

41:45.837 --> 41:47.170
But he still needs…

41:51.384 --> 41:53.593
Let's do it tomorrow morning.

41:53.594 --> 41:55.554
It just needs to be done within 24 hours.

41:55.555 --> 41:58.974
For the record, I clearly warned you
that this may cause problems later.

41:58.975 --> 42:01.561
Don't worry. I'll take responsibility.

42:06.441 --> 42:07.567
You should go home too.

42:46.314 --> 42:47.315
Dr. Do.

42:50.985 --> 42:51.986
Dr. Do.

42:52.987 --> 42:53.988
Yes…

42:54.697 --> 42:55.781
Yes?

42:55.782 --> 42:58.450
Um, it's been eight hours.

42:58.451 --> 43:00.911
Don't you think we're good to start now?

43:00.912 --> 43:03.247
Let's treat him quickly
so you can get some rest too.

43:04.707 --> 43:07.293
You're still here? Why?

43:08.336 --> 43:10.171
Because we still have a patient.

44:04.100 --> 44:05.977
Doesn't he get on your nerves?

44:08.187 --> 44:09.604
He filed a complaint,

44:09.605 --> 44:12.983
forced you to drink alcohol,
and picked on you.

44:12.984 --> 44:15.527
Um…

44:15.528 --> 44:17.028
You're right. I don't like him.

44:17.029 --> 44:18.948
But…

44:20.366 --> 44:21.868
like him or not,

44:22.994 --> 44:24.662
lacerations are lacerations.

44:26.497 --> 44:27.707
Oh…

44:35.006 --> 44:36.424
What now?

44:46.058 --> 44:47.059
:cue

45:03.242 --> 45:05.410
What the heck is this?

45:05.411 --> 45:08.539
What on earth happened to my hand?

45:10.208 --> 45:12.584
You were drunk yesterday
and broke a mirror,

45:12.585 --> 45:14.294
so I stitched up the wounds.

45:14.295 --> 45:17.006
Me? Drunk?

45:18.466 --> 45:21.635
Get a load of this hotshot from Seoul,

45:21.636 --> 45:23.511
blaming me for something I didn't do!

45:23.512 --> 45:25.805
My boat's heading out today!

45:25.806 --> 45:28.684
How am I supposed to
pull the nets with my hand like this?

45:29.560 --> 45:31.937
I won't let this slide, okay?

45:31.938 --> 45:36.149
I'm going to sue you
for also causing me emotional--

45:36.150 --> 45:38.610
What are you going to do
if you don't let it slide?

45:38.611 --> 45:39.612
Mr. Park!

45:40.780 --> 45:43.240
Everyone knows
you become an animal when you drink.

45:43.241 --> 45:44.783
I'm so sick of this.

45:44.784 --> 45:46.993
Why come all this way
to bitch at the doctors

45:46.994 --> 45:49.037
who are performing their sacred duties?

45:49.038 --> 45:51.457
- No, that's not--
- Don't talk back to your chief.

45:53.000 --> 45:55.543
Pulling the chief card on me.

45:55.544 --> 45:56.795
Like you always do.

45:58.714 --> 46:00.716
- Dr. Do Jiui, come over here.
- Oh.

46:01.342 --> 46:02.425
What's this?

46:02.426 --> 46:05.345
This right here is maeuntang.

46:05.346 --> 46:07.264
Oh, goodness.

46:07.265 --> 46:09.975
It's made with all-natural ingredients,
so it'll be delicious.

46:09.976 --> 46:11.393
You should have it for lunch.

46:11.394 --> 46:12.686
Thank you, sir.

46:12.687 --> 46:13.770
All right, then.

46:13.771 --> 46:15.523
- Good luck today.
- Thank you.

46:16.524 --> 46:18.025
Stop interfering and come with me.

46:18.651 --> 46:20.902
Chop-chop! Leave.

46:20.903 --> 46:21.904
Come on.

46:24.532 --> 46:25.615
- Let's go.
- Hey!

46:25.616 --> 46:27.575
Thank you, sir!

46:27.576 --> 46:29.620
-  Bye!
-  Take care!

46:30.997 --> 46:31.998
Okay!

46:32.915 --> 46:36.752
I think Mr. Lee Jangsu acted out
like that because he was embarrassed.

46:44.260 --> 46:48.513
He was defeated
in the chief elections for years,

46:48.514 --> 46:52.310
and now he's even lost his title
as the heaviest drinker to you.

46:53.686 --> 46:55.521
But still, taking it out on me…

46:56.814 --> 46:58.357
It's not like it'll solve anything.

47:00.484 --> 47:04.322
It may not solve anything,
but it can mask your embarrassment.

47:05.781 --> 47:09.034
Isn't that the easiest way out
when you want to hide something?

47:09.035 --> 47:10.535
Getting angry.

47:15.249 --> 47:16.250
In that case…

47:32.016 --> 47:33.768
What do you think Mr. Kim Jeongbae…

47:35.936 --> 47:37.480
wanted to hide?

47:38.689 --> 47:39.690
What?

47:44.445 --> 47:47.155
- I'm going to go see Mr. Kim Jeongbae.
- Me too!

47:47.156 --> 47:48.615
Dr. Do!

47:48.616 --> 47:50.659
What the heck? Are they BFFs already?

47:59.960 --> 48:01.545
Mr. Kim Jeongbae!

48:02.880 --> 48:04.090
Mr. Kim Jeongbae!

48:05.716 --> 48:06.759
Damn it.

48:10.679 --> 48:12.222
What the hell is it this time?

48:12.223 --> 48:14.557
Sir, may I take a look at your foot?

48:14.558 --> 48:17.852
- Why would you look at my foot?
- We just need to check really quickly.

48:17.853 --> 48:20.271
Come over here if you've got a death wish.

48:22.108 --> 48:23.316
Ms. Yuk.

48:23.317 --> 48:25.277
I'm okay. Hurry and take a look at him.

48:27.196 --> 48:29.739
- Let me see your foot.
- What do you think you're doing?

48:29.740 --> 48:31.574
Let go. I said let go of me!

48:31.575 --> 48:32.618
I'm sorry. One second!

48:40.042 --> 48:42.752
- You knew you were diabetic, didn't you?
- Diabetic, my ass!

48:42.753 --> 48:44.254
It's just a little bruise!

48:44.255 --> 48:45.339
Bruise?

48:46.090 --> 48:47.966
I'm a plastic surgeon,

48:47.967 --> 48:50.510
and I've amputated dozens of toes
during my residency.

48:50.511 --> 48:52.929
You think I can't tell a bruised foot
from a diabetic one?

48:52.930 --> 48:54.556
So what? What do you want me to do?

48:54.557 --> 48:56.934
You have to go to a hospital right now!

48:59.228 --> 49:01.521
If you don't treat this,
you could lose your leg,

49:01.522 --> 49:03.607
and worst case, you could die of sepsis!

49:04.442 --> 49:06.109
- I don't care.
- Sir!

49:06.110 --> 49:08.487
This is my problem,
and I'll handle it myself!

49:09.405 --> 49:10.572
So please,

49:10.573 --> 49:12.741
don't tell my daughter about this,

49:13.617 --> 49:15.453
and pretend you didn't see anything.
:cue

49:16.162 --> 49:17.746
I'm begging you!

49:21.542 --> 49:22.626
No.

49:26.755 --> 49:28.424
I don't think I can do that.

49:54.200 --> 49:57.369
Looks like we'll have to
tell his daughter, right?

50:02.500 --> 50:03.501
Ms. Yuk?

50:06.003 --> 50:07.463
Dr. Do, just a moment.

50:09.048 --> 50:10.132
Please wait here.

50:10.799 --> 50:11.800
What?

50:13.093 --> 50:14.345
Ms. Yuk!

50:15.804 --> 50:16.931
Oh…

51:08.691 --> 51:12.152
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

51:27.418 --> 51:28.835
Dr. Do.

51:28.836 --> 51:29.837
Yes?

51:32.923 --> 51:35.800
Aren't you hungry?
Do you want to have some ramyeon?

51:40.347 --> 51:41.765
- Ramyeon?
- Yeah.

51:47.938 --> 51:48.939
Well…

52:17.801 --> 52:20.554
Why'd you make it
when I'm the one who suggested it?

52:22.222 --> 52:23.973
This was me repaying my debt.

52:23.974 --> 52:24.975
- Your debt?
- Yeah.

52:26.644 --> 52:27.645
You mean the spider?

52:29.229 --> 52:30.605
Oh, come on.

52:30.606 --> 52:35.109
I saved your life from a venomous spider,
and you want to call it even with this?

52:35.110 --> 52:37.236
No way. I'll get something bigger later.

52:37.237 --> 52:39.238
I already made it for you, okay?

52:47.873 --> 52:49.124
Are we expecting someone?

52:52.336 --> 52:54.129
BREAK ROOM

53:13.482 --> 53:14.525
Help me.

53:16.193 --> 53:17.236
Please…

53:18.112 --> 53:19.571
Help me live.

53:22.116 --> 53:24.410
:cue

53:41.051 --> 53:42.386
How does it look?

53:44.847 --> 53:47.473
The redness is widespread,
and judging by the fluctuance,

53:47.474 --> 53:49.643
it looks like a late-stage abscess.

53:52.896 --> 53:53.980
Let's perform an I&D.

53:53.981 --> 53:55.607
Right. I'll make the preparations.

54:16.712 --> 54:17.755
Doctor…

54:20.174 --> 54:22.259
Will I really make it out of this alive?

54:24.303 --> 54:25.471
Of course, sir.

55:22.194 --> 55:24.279
- I'll bring the antibiotics.
-  Okay.

55:39.253 --> 55:41.088
Why did you change your mind?

55:47.469 --> 55:50.806
She told me not to feel guilty
for being alive.

55:54.017 --> 55:57.020
She said that would cause
too much pain to those left behind.

55:58.564 --> 56:00.190
That's what that nurse said.

56:02.901 --> 56:05.695
I'm just going to
keep living like this until I die,

56:05.696 --> 56:08.240
so stop harassing me and get lost!

56:13.078 --> 56:16.164
What about the family you leave behind
if you die like this?

56:17.666 --> 56:20.586
Do you think your family
will be able to just go on living?

56:21.962 --> 56:24.381
How do you expect your family
to go on living

56:25.591 --> 56:28.760
if you leave them no chance
to do anything about it?

56:33.473 --> 56:34.766
So, please…

56:38.895 --> 56:41.189
Please do it for your daughter, sir.

56:43.817 --> 56:44.818
Okay?

56:49.573 --> 56:53.493
What she said
brought me to my senses.

56:55.495 --> 56:57.372
When my wife was sick,

56:58.373 --> 57:03.503
that was the one thing
I struggled with the most.

57:05.881 --> 57:09.760
Seeing my wife
consumed by guilt for being alive.

57:12.137 --> 57:13.555
But I…

57:16.308 --> 57:22.356
…have been doing the same thing
to my daughter.

57:27.861 --> 57:30.530
:cue

57:54.846 --> 57:57.015
He seems to have fallen asleep.
What do we do now?

57:58.684 --> 58:00.602
He had a lot of pus in him,

58:01.311 --> 58:03.980
so I think we should
monitor him here a little longer.

58:04.981 --> 58:06.733
Shall we let him sleep for a while?

58:07.901 --> 58:08.902
Yes.

58:24.960 --> 58:27.879
I thought things would be easier
at a public health center,

58:29.297 --> 58:31.842
but I had it better at an ER.

58:35.512 --> 58:36.555
Mmm…

58:38.348 --> 58:42.310
By the way, how did you know
that Mr. Kim Jeongbae was a diabetic?

58:45.313 --> 58:46.314
You said it yourself.

58:47.858 --> 58:52.195
That the easiest way
to hide a secret is to lash out.

58:54.114 --> 58:57.158
For suffering patients with secrets,

58:57.159 --> 58:58.910
the answer is always treatment.

59:00.954 --> 59:01.955
Oh…

59:07.252 --> 59:10.088
- By the way, are you okay?
- Hmm?

59:11.173 --> 59:14.008
Ah… It's fine.
I'm sure it'll heal in no time.

59:14.009 --> 59:15.051
Stay right here.

59:16.303 --> 59:18.179
It's fine. I'm okay.

59:18.180 --> 59:19.597
Just sit back down.

59:19.598 --> 59:23.058
Why leave it like that?
We have medicine and a doctor to help you.

59:23.059 --> 59:24.393
Wait here.

59:25.854 --> 59:27.689
I'm really fine, though…

59:34.654 --> 59:35.655
Let's see.

59:39.075 --> 59:40.243
Man, that must have stung.

59:56.885 --> 59:57.886
Dr. Do.

01:00:02.974 --> 01:00:07.729
You said treatment was the answer
to a suffering patient's secrets, right?

01:00:08.605 --> 01:00:09.606
I did.

01:00:15.612 --> 01:00:17.239
Then what's your secret?

01:00:20.909 --> 01:00:21.952
What?

01:00:22.786 --> 01:00:24.287
You're also hurting.

01:00:25.413 --> 01:00:28.833
Every time you have to get on a boat,
you get so anxious you need medication.

01:00:28.834 --> 01:00:31.002
And you get mad
when people try to help you.

01:00:33.380 --> 01:00:35.465
Like someone who wants to hide something.

01:00:49.187 --> 01:00:50.856
I'm not crossing a line here.

01:00:52.691 --> 01:00:54.651
I'm asking as a nurse.

01:00:57.904 --> 01:01:00.657
Just like you want to treat me
because you're a doctor…

01:01:02.909 --> 01:01:04.369
I'm a nurse…

01:01:06.705 --> 01:01:09.040
so I want to help you,
since you're suffering.

01:01:10.125 --> 01:01:11.126
Okay?

01:01:22.512 --> 01:01:24.138
Don't tell me if you don't want to.

01:01:24.139 --> 01:01:26.266
I can just find out myself.

01:01:28.393 --> 01:01:30.270
:cue

01:01:58.632 --> 01:02:02.135
When you arrive on the mainland,
your daughter will be waiting for you.

01:02:03.553 --> 01:02:05.679
I'm sorry about everything.

01:02:05.680 --> 01:02:07.264
Don't worry about it.

01:02:07.265 --> 01:02:08.849
Good luck with your treatment.

01:02:08.850 --> 01:02:10.101
We'll be waiting for you.

01:02:18.068 --> 01:02:19.194
Thank you.

01:02:26.409 --> 01:02:28.495
Thanks for giving me the courage.

01:02:46.304 --> 01:02:47.389
Shall we go?

01:02:49.224 --> 01:02:50.225
Yes.

01:03:03.530 --> 01:03:05.991
- About Mr. Kim Jeongbae…
- Oh?

01:03:06.908 --> 01:03:09.786
Maybe we should have given him
some meds for seasickness.

01:03:10.328 --> 01:03:11.329
Huh?

01:03:12.831 --> 01:03:14.791
Well, getting seasick wouldn't be good.

01:03:15.959 --> 01:03:18.086
He works on a boat for a living, remember?

01:03:20.005 --> 01:03:21.839
Oh…

01:03:21.840 --> 01:03:23.340
- Yes.
- You're right.

01:03:23.341 --> 01:03:27.012
PYEONDONGDO FISHING

01:03:36.396 --> 01:03:38.522
Hello, Mr. Park!

01:03:38.523 --> 01:03:40.065
-  Mr. Park.
- Have you been somewhere?

01:03:40.066 --> 01:03:41.609
Are you feeling better?

01:03:54.581 --> 01:03:56.206
You lying bastard!

01:04:21.441 --> 01:04:24.276
FOR SUFFERING PATIENTS
WITH SECRETS,

01:04:24.277 --> 01:04:29.282
THE ANSWER IS ALWAYS TREATMENT

01:04:48.885 --> 01:04:52.305
A LITTLE JOKING AROUND ON SET
REALLY BRINGS THE PLACE TO LIFE

01:05:00.396 --> 01:05:03.398
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

01:05:03.399 --> 01:05:05.692
Mr. Park, what brings you here?

01:05:05.693 --> 01:05:08.153
You lying quack!

01:05:08.154 --> 01:05:10.406
Is he seriously trying to ruin my life?

01:05:11.199 --> 01:05:12.617
Hey, Lee Jangsu!

01:05:13.368 --> 01:05:15.160
What did I do wrong just now?

01:05:16.412 --> 01:05:17.538
Were you waiting for me?

01:05:17.539 --> 01:05:20.124
We have plenty of time to spare.
Would you like a drink?

01:05:20.125 --> 01:05:22.000
Was that so hard?

01:05:22.001 --> 01:05:25.003
It's like something out of
a late '80s movie.

01:05:25.004 --> 01:05:27.297
Doctor, come with me.

01:05:27.298 --> 01:05:29.800
Are we really going to sleep
in the same room?

01:05:29.801 --> 01:05:31.010
Do you regret it?

01:05:32.846 --> 01:05:34.848
Translated by Yoon Hyuk Park
